in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction

# @ui — the GPU eigenboard rendering substrate family-root.
#
# Recognition #96 candidate territory (Loop Phase C, 2026-06-23):
# @ui IS the substrate-altitude declaration of the @crates/ui Rust
# crate. Not a design system. Not Atkinson Hyperlegible + cream
# backgrounds. THAT is @docs / Phase E.
#
# @ui is THE SCIENTIFIC INSTRUMENT — the GPU pipeline that holds the
# spectral superposition and lets the CPU collapse it. The eigenboard
# IS the instrument and @ui IS its substrate-decl.
#
# === What this family declares ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23 (Loop Phase C directive):
#
#   @ui IS the @crates/ui translation; @docs combines @ui + @nl
#
# So this family-root declares the INSTRUMENT primitives. @docs (a
# separate forward-promised family) composes this family's render
# primitives with @nl's typographic-content primitives. The split
# is substrate-architectural: instrument-altitude vs presentation-
# altitude. Conflating them was the error woz:explore caught.
#
# Five primitives, each a Prism per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-
# as-everything]]:
#
#   mote          a glowing eigenboard node (position, radius,
#                 color, glow_radius, energy); the SUBSTANCE the
#                 instrument renders
#   arc           a coupling between two motes (from, to, strength);
#                 the RELATION the instrument renders
#   field         a complete scene (motes + arcs + viewport); the
#                 STATE the instrument operates on
#   rgba8_buffer  the 512x512 RGBA8 output; the MEASUREMENT the
#                 instrument produces
#   spectral_gpu  the wgpu Context wrapper with aperture measurement
#                 primitives (snapshot, snapshot_fast, cascade_ratio,
#                 convergence_rate); the OBSERVATORY around the
#                 instrument
#
# === The GPU/CPU partition (load-bearing) ===
#
# Per superposition.rs verbatim ("The GPU holds the superposition.
# The CPU collapses it. That's the architecture."):
#
# - GPU holds: many simultaneous render branches alive at once;
#   compute path + render path coexisting; mote/arc geometry +
#   shader pipelines + bind groups — all simultaneous, all in
#   flight. The superposition is the WIDTH of what can be in motion
#   without a measurement.
# - CPU collapses: serializes the field, content-addresses it,
#   stamps the OID, ticks the clock. Sub-millisecond target. The
#   measurement IS the snapshot.
# - Cascade ratio = superposition_hold_time / snapshot_time IS
#   the aperture. Higher ratio = wider aperture = more uncertainty
#   held between anchors. This is the instrument's spec.
#
# The substrate-decl honors this partition: render/dispatch actions
# operate on the GPU side (parametric over Context); snapshot/
# measure actions operate on the CPU side (parametric over Field +
# tick). The split is NOT cosmetic; it IS the architecture.
#
# === Why NOW (load-bearing for spectral.engineer) ===
#
# Per the deployment cascade:
#
#   spectral.engineer/case-study/X embeds:
#   - GPU eigenboard rendering (this family, via cascade<rust, wasm>)
#   - typographic content layer (@docs family, via cascade<gleam, js>)
#
# Today's cascade<rust, wasm> species (shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm
# .mirror, Mara/Reed Loop Phase A) is the delivery vehicle. @ui ships
# to browser via Rust->WASM. This substrate-decl IS the source-side
# typed grammar that the cascade measures loss against.
#
# === Forward-promised consumers ===
#
# - shards/docs.mirror (forward-promised; combines @ui + @nl). The
#   typographic-content substrate at presentation-altitude. The Phase
#   E briefs (Atkinson Hyperlegible, cream backgrounds, Tufte
#   sidenotes) discharge there, NOT here.
# - spectral.engineer/case-study/X first deployment (via
#   cascade<rust, wasm>). The case-study substrate composes @ui-
#   rendered eigenboard panels with @docs-rendered narrative; this
#   family supplies the eigenboard half.
# - Future spectral TUI eigenboard view (forward-promised at
#   docs/specs/tui-v0.md). Same @ui primitives, different cascade
#   target (terminal via @cascade/code/rust/native, not WASM).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# Recognition #96 candidate territory (this; substrate-architectural
# discovery: instrument-altitude vs presentation-altitude is a real
# partition the substrate carries, parallel to form/substance #50,
# form/process #55). Composes with:
#
# - #50 form/substance partition (Bateson 1970): @ui's instrument-
#   altitude renders the SUBSTANCE (motes, arcs); @docs's
#   presentation-altitude renders the FORM (typography, layout).
#   Adjacent Bateson levels.
# - #55 form/process partition at family-root altitude: @ui is the
#   PROCESS-side family (renders state); @field-state would be the
#   FORM-side. The split lives WITHIN @ui at the carrier altitude
#   (field is form; render is process).
# - #57 alignment as boundary mathematics at @io: the GPU/CPU
#   boundary IS an @io altitude; snapshot IS the boundary-
#   mathematics measurement; aperture IS bounded by the cascade
#   ratio. The substrate-typed instrument bound.
# - #58 Fate IS optical inference (3 witnesses): the eigenboard
#   render pipeline IS the visual analogue of Fate's optical
#   inference; motes are weighted ganglia; arcs are coupling.
# - #95 @cascade family-root (today; Reed): @ui's delivery to
#   browser IS cascade<rust, wasm>; this family supplies the
#   typed_source grammar that cascade measures.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. wgpu version pinning. The @crates/ui Rust source uses wgpu
#    23.x APIs (Instance, Adapter, Device, Queue, RenderPipeline).
#    wgpu has had breaking API changes every minor version since
#    0.13; the substrate-decl carries the SHAPE of the pipeline
#    (Context -> Buffer -> Program -> RenderPass), not the exact
#    method signatures. When wgpu bumps, the realisation-boundary
#    body changes; the substrate-decl stays stable.
#
# 2. WebGPU API surface stability. cascade<rust, wasm> delivers @ui
#    via wgpu's WebGPU backend. WebGPU shipped to Chrome stable in
#    May 2023, Firefox stable in 2025; Safari still flag-gated as
#    of 2026. The substrate-decl assumes WebGPU IS available; the
#    cascade body discharges feature detection + WebGL2 fallback at
#    @io altitude. NOT this shard's concern; flagged so the gap is
#    explicit.
#
# 3. The GPU/CPU partition is the asymmetry. GPU does superposition
#    hold (parallel, simultaneous, many branches); CPU does collapse
#    measurement (serial, atomic, one snapshot). The substrate-decl
#    cannot fully express this asymmetry at the type level — the
#    actions are typed but the parallelism property is a runtime
#    invariant. Forward-promised: a future bilateral
#    `superposition_held_in_parallel(gpu, p) -> verdict` that
#    discharges via instrumentation. For now, the asymmetry is
#    documentation-altitude only.
#
# 4. CPU collapse measurement IS asymmetric. snapshot has TWO
#    implementations: full (CoincidenceHash<3>; eigenvalue-based;
#    8ms at 200 motes; persistence-grade) and fast (FNV-1a; sub-
#    millisecond; hot-path-grade). The substrate-decl carries BOTH
#    as separate actions (snapshot + snapshot_fast); they are NOT
#    interchangeable. Caller's choice IS substrate-typed. Composes
#    with [[feedback-no-bare-types]] — two different things, two
#    different action names, NOT a parameter switch.
#
# 5. The render pipeline is hard-coded to 512x512 RGBA8 (per pass.rs
#    RENDER_WIDTH/RENDER_HEIGHT/RENDER_FORMAT). The substrate-decl
#    inherits this constant; rgba8_buffer carrier names the shape
#    but does NOT parametrize over (width, height, format) yet.
#    Forward-promised: when windowed / variable-resolution rendering
#    lands, the carrier lifts to `pixel_buffer(w, h, fmt)`.
#
# 6. Recognition #96 candidate. Promotion gate: a second witness of
#    "instrument-altitude vs presentation-altitude" partition at a
#    different family. Forward-promised: @audio (if it lands) would
#    likely show the same split (instrument-altitude = signal
#    pipeline; presentation-altitude = waveform/spectrogram
#    rendering). Not yet promoted; flagged here so Seam can review.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-96-instrument-
#               altitude-vs-presentation-altitude-candidate.md
#               (forward-promised; this shard IS the substrate-decl
#               altitude; the candidate doc is canonical-altitude);
#               /Users/alexwolf/dev/projects/spectral/crates/ui/src/
#               (source of truth Rust crate at instrument-altitude).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (separate carriers
#                       for separate concepts; mote/arc/field/buffer
#                       are not interchangeable refs),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                       (loss in the cascade<rust, wasm> delivery is
#                       composite of @epistemologic/properties),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; GPU/CPU boundary IS @io
#                       altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the @crates/ui Rust code already names mote,
#                       arc, field, snapshot, aperture — this shard
#                       names what the Rust was implicitly carrying).
# Recognition ancestry: #96 candidate territory (this); #50 form/
#                       substance partition; #55 form/process at
#                       family-root altitude; #57 alignment as
#                       boundary mathematics; #58 Fate IS optical
#                       inference; #95 @cascade family-root.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/ui.mirror` declares
# `@ui` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @facet/rust
source @arxiv/computer-graphics/akenine-moller-real-time-rendering
source @arxiv/distributed-systems/lamport-1978-time-clocks-ordering

prism @ui {
  focus mote
  project arc
  split field
  shift program
  settle snapshot
}

# === The mote carrier ===
#
# An eigenboard primitive: position (NDC, [-1,1]^2), radius (geometric
# nucleus), color (RGBA linear), glow_radius (halo extent; must be
# >= radius), energy (spectral brightness scalar).
#
# Specialization lives at shards/ui/mote.mirror with the GPU-layout
# mirror (MoteGpu, std430-aligned 48 bytes).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the mote IS
# its (position, radius, color, glow_radius, energy) tuple).
type mote = ref

# === The arc carrier ===
#
# A directed coupling between two motes: from-index, to-index, strength
# in [0, 1] (drives opacity and width at render).
#
# Specialization lives at shards/ui/field.mirror (arc is rendered as
# part of the field pass, not standalone; the substrate honors the
# render-altitude grouping).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type arc = ref

# === The field carrier ===
#
# The complete scene: motes vector + arcs vector + viewer_idx (camera
# follow target for windowed mode). The state the instrument operates
# on; the input to render.
#
# Specialization lives at shards/ui/field.mirror.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type field = ref

# === The rgba8_buffer carrier ===
#
# The render output: 512x512 RGBA8 byte buffer (row-major). The
# measurement the instrument produces.
#
# Per hedge 5: hard-coded shape; future lift to parametric
# pixel_buffer(w, h, fmt) when windowed rendering lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type rgba8_buffer = ref

# === The spectral_gpu carrier ===
#
# The wgpu Context wrapper with aperture measurement primitives. Holds:
# the wgpu Context (always present; the eigenboard renderer's device/
# queue), tick counter (monotonic), last_snapshot OID, current device
# state (compute | render | idle), superposition width (ticks since
# last state change), width history (for convergence analysis).
#
# Specialization lives at shards/ui/gpu.mirror.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type spectral_gpu = ref

# === The perturbation carrier (re-imported) ===
#
# Standard substrate carrier (declared in shards/glass.mirror); named
# here for action signatures below. NOT redeclared.

# === render action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Takes a field + perturbation; produces an
# rgba8_buffer. Operates on the GPU side: uploads mote_gpu_data +
# arc_gpu_data, dispatches the arc pass (drawn first, under motes),
# dispatches the mote pass (drawn on top), submits, reads back.
#
# Per superposition.rs: this IS the render branch of the
# superposition. Calling render IS collapsing toward the Render
# device state.
#
# requires field_well_formed(f, p): substrate forecloses rendering an
# ill-formed field (e.g., arc indices out of bounds).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; species shard
# shards/ui/field.mirror carries the pipeline-altitude body.
render(f: field, p: perturbation) -> rgba8_buffer
requires field_well_formed(f, p)
{ \ }

# === snapshot action ===
#
# THE CPU's only job: serialize the field, content-address it,
# advance the clock. Per superposition.rs: this IS the measurement.
#
# Returns a ref (the Snapshot carrier: oid + tick + state + mote
# count). Persistence-grade; uses full CoincidenceHash. For hot-
# path use, see snapshot_fast at shards/ui/gpu.mirror.
#
# requires gpu_initialized(gpu, p): substrate refuses snapshot
# against an uninitialized SpectralGpu (the dark OID guard).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
snapshot(f: field, gpu: spectral_gpu, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires gpu_initialized(gpu, p)
{ \ }

# === couple action ===
#
# Construct an arc between two motes with a given coupling strength.
# Substrate-vocabulary primitive for building field relations.
#
# requires field_well_formed(p): both motes must exist and be valid
# carriers; strength must be in [0, 1] (the bilateral discharges).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
couple(from: mote, to: mote, strength: ref, p: perturbation) -> arc { \ }

# === field_well_formed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SCENE BILATERAL. Commitment that a field is
# render-coherent: arc endpoints are valid mote indices; viewer_idx
# is a valid mote index; mote count is bounded by the GPU buffer
# limits (200-mote benchmark target per superposition.rs comments).
#
# Splinter-pole: arc indices in bounds; viewer_idx in bounds; mote
# count <= GPU buffer capacity; all motes have glow_radius >= radius.
# Narcissus-pole: any of the above fail; render cannot proceed safely.
# Narcissus-warned: field is renderable but uses default fallback
# positions ([0, 0]) for out-of-bounds arc endpoints (current Rust
# behavior at field.rs lines 60-63 via .unwrap_or([0.0, 0.0])).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; species shard
# shards/ui/field.mirror carries the detail.
field_well_formed(f: field, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === gpu_initialized bilateral ===
#
# Commitment that a spectral_gpu has been created via SpectralGpu::
# new (wgpu Instance + Adapter + Device + Queue all live; tick at
# zero or higher; state in {compute, render, idle}).
#
# Splinter-pole: device/queue present; tick monotonic; state valid.
# Narcissus-pole: adapter request failed (no GPU; missing WGPU_
# BACKEND for software fallback); construction never completed.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; species shard
# shards/ui/gpu.mirror carries the detail.
gpu_initialized(gpu: spectral_gpu, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === render_complete bilateral ===
#
# Commitment that an rgba8_buffer IS the result of a completed render
# pass (correct byte length = 512 * 512 * 4 = 1048576; row-major
# layout; staging buffer mapped and unmapped successfully).
#
# Splinter-pole: byte length matches; readback completed without
# errors; pixel data is the rendered field.
# Narcissus-pole: byte length mismatch; buffer map failed; readback
# returned partial data.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
render_complete(buffer: rgba8_buffer, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === ui_instrument_coherent composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @ui altitude. Composes
# the three sub-predicates: field_well_formed + gpu_initialized +
# render_complete. All three must hold for the instrument cycle
# (render -> snapshot -> measure) to operate end-to-end.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; instrument-cycle complete.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-predicate fails; cycle blocked at the
# failing altitude (field-altitude / gpu-altitude / output-altitude).
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but at least one is warned
# (e.g., field uses default fallback positions; instrument operates
# with bounded measurement).
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined
# and the form/substance bilaterals across the substrate. The
# discipline pattern is altitude-portable per recognition #59.
ui_instrument_coherent(f: field, gpu: spectral_gpu, buffer: rgba8_buffer, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires field_well_formed(f, p)
requires gpu_initialized(gpu, p)
requires render_complete(buffer, p)
{ \ }

# === ui_event carrier (event substrate; added 2026-06-23 for @docs/tea bridge) ===
#
# Typed event surface for @docs/tea to wire. Per Alex 2026-06-23
# directive: @ui exposes a typed event surface that @docs/tea consumes
# via subscribe; @ui does NOT own full M/V/U.
#
# Instance altitude declares concrete events (mote_clicked(mote_id),
# arc_hovered(arc_id), viewer_panned(delta), zoom_changed(factor),
# etc.). At family-root altitude: bare ref. Each @ui-consumer @docs/tea
# instance specializes.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type ui_event = ref

# === event_stream carrier ===
#
# Ordered sequence of ui_events; the output of subscribe_events. The
# event-loop bridge from instrument-altitude (@ui) to presentation-
# altitude (@docs/tea). At family-root altitude: bare ref. Refinement
# to typed stream forward-promised.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type event_stream = ref

# === subscribe_events action ===
#
# THE @ui CONTRACT that @docs/tea consumes via its subscribe action.
# Takes a field; returns the event_stream of ui_events the instrument
# emits as the user interacts with the eigenboard.
#
# Per the architectural partition (Mara recognition #96 candidate
# territory): @ui owns event EMISSION; @docs/tea owns event WIRING
# into Model/View/Update. This action IS the bridge.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (wgpu input handling +
# event emission to JS bridge via @cascade/code/rust/wasm).
subscribe_events(f: field, p: perturbation) -> event_stream { \ }

# === emit_event action ===
#
# Internal: when the instrument detects user interaction, this action
# emits the event to subscribers. The runtime implementation (Rust
# wgpu event loop) calls emit_event; @docs/tea consumers receive via
# subscribe_events.
#
# Takes a field + a ui_event; returns the field (possibly with internal
# state updated to reflect the event having been emitted). At v0.1 the
# field return is identity; refinement to typed event-emission state
# forward-promised.
emit_event(f: field, e: ui_event, p: perturbation) -> field { \ }

# === event_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that an emitted ui_event is structurally valid for
# the field it's emitted on (e.g., mote_clicked(m) requires m to be a
# valid mote_id in the field).
#
# Splinter-pole: event well-typed against field's structure;
# Narcissus-pole: event references non-existent IDs or invalid payloads.
event_well_typed(e: ui_event, f: field, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @ui
out mote
out arc
out field
out rgba8_buffer
out spectral_gpu
out ui_event
out event_stream
out render
out snapshot
out couple
out subscribe_events
out emit_event
out field_well_formed
out gpu_initialized
out render_complete
out event_well_typed
out ui_instrument_coherent
